ternet_y_repositorios/github_repos/superna9999__pyamlboot/pyamlboot-master/ADNL.md) and [`experimento/06_internet_y_repositorios/github_repos/superna9999__pyamlboot/pyamlboot-master/adnl.py`](file:///c:/Users/andre/OneDrive/Desktop/xview/experimento/06_internet_y_repositorios/github_repos/superna9999__pyamlboot/pyamlboot-master/adnl.py).\n\n---\n\n### 3. Key Findings (BREAKTHROUGH: WHY THE BOX HAS GREEN LED AND HOW IT IS CONNECTED RIGHT NOW)\n1. **Why `[1/12] fastboot flash env env_unlocked.img` Prevented Linux from Booting:**\n   - In the original [`B866V2-FlashATV12_Evoca_DESOFUSCADO.bat`](file:///c:/Users/andre/OneDrive/Desktop/xview/experimento/09_analisis_archivos_usuario/B866V2-FlashATV12_Evoca_DESOFUSCADO.bat), **`env` is NEVER flashed!** It only runs `fastboot oem 'setenv lock 10100000;save`.\n   - In [`BLOQUES_ASCII_COMPLETOS_SESION.txt`](file:///c:/Users/andre/OneDrive/Desktop/xview/experimento/14_MONITOREO_EN_VIVO_SMARTTY/BLOQUES_ASCII_COMPLETOS_SESION.txt) (lines 519, 546, 564), ZTE's U-Boot (`U-Boot 2015.01-g220e992`) boots Android 12 using:\n     - `ztebsp: cmdT = imgread kernel boot ${loadaddr};bootm ${loadaddr}`\n     - Where ZTE's genuine `loadaddr` is **`0x03080000`** (`## Booting Android Image at 0x03080000 ...`), because the gzip-compressed Android 12 kernel inside `boot.img` decompresses to physical RAM at **`0x01080000` (`kernel loaded at 0x01080000, end = 0x028bb008`)**!\n   - However, [`env_unlocked.img`](file:///c:/Users/andre/OneDrive/Desktop/xview/programa%20perfecto/5_FIRMWARE_SEGURO_B866V2/env_unlocked.img) (which `ProgramaPerfecto.cs` flashed to `env`) set:\n     - **`loadaddr=0x1080000`** (`0x01080000`)!\n     - **`storeboot=imgread kernel boot ${loadaddr}; bootm ${loadaddr};`**\n     - **`update=run usb_burning; run sdc_burning`** and **`usb_burning=update 1000`**!\n   - When `bootm 0x1080000` runs, it tries to gunzip the kernel from `0x01080000` onto itself at `0x01080000`, which corrupts the gzip stream (`inflate() returned -3`) and