fastboot` (`ADNL_REPLY_OKAY`, `ADNL_REPLY_FAIL`, `ADNL_REPLY_INFO`, `ADNL_REPLY_DATA`)!\n   - By reading `ADNL.md` and `adnl.py`, we can send U-Boot commands (`oem` / `cb_oem_cmd` / `setenv loadaddr 0x03080000; saveenv; fastboot` / `reset`) directly to `USB\\VID_1B8E&PID_C004\\00199321C9402A2200000000` right now over WinUSB without the user even touching the box!\n\n---\n\n### 4. Errors & Fixes\n- **Error 1: Box `Z41221040106995` stayed on solid green LED with no HDMI output after completing the 13-partition flash:**\n  - *Root cause:* `[1/12] fastboot flash env env_unlocked.img` wrote `loadaddr=0x1080000` into `/dev/block/env`. Because the Android 12 kernel in `boot.img` decompresses into `0x01080000`, `bootm 0x1080000` overwrites itself during gunzip (`inflate() returned -3`), fails to boot Linux, and falls through to `update 1000`, parking the box in Amlogic `DNL` / `ADNL` mode (`USB\\VID_1B8E&PID_C004`).\n- **Error 2: `DnlProbe` `CreateFile` returned Win32 Error `5` (`ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED`) on `VID_1B8E&PID_C004`:**\n  - *Root cause:* `adb.exe` background server holds an exclusive handle on `{f72fe0d4-cbcb-407d-8814-9ed673d0dd6b}` WinUSB devices with `Class_FF&SubClass_42`. Killing `adb.exe` (`Stop-Process -Name adb -Force`) releases the WinUSB handle so our C# `WinUsb` client can open `VID_1B8E&PID_C004` immediately.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Active Context\n- **Connected Hardware Right Now:**\n  - Box `Z41221040106995` is **actively connected right now** via USB Male-to-Male cable as **`USB\\VID_1B8E&PID_C004\\00199321C9402A2200000000` (`DNL`)**!\n  - It ALREADY has all Android 12 liberated partitions (`boot.img`, `bootloader.img`, `dtb.img`, `dtbo.img`, `logo.img`, `param.img`, `conf.img`, `oem.img`, `vbmeta.img`, and **`super.img` `1.88 GB` `DMC.v2.25`**) flashed to its eMMC!\n  - The **ONLY** thing keeping it from booting into `DMC.v2.25` with HDMI video right now is `loadaddr=0x1080000` in `/dev/block/env` (and `5_FIRMWARE_SEGURO_B866V2\\recovery.img` which should m