{"step_index":1351,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-05T14:26:09Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-05T08:26:09-06:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-05T08:26:09-06:00\nShowing lines 1-40 of 40\n1: <!--- SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0 OR MIT -->\n2: \n3: # Description of burning firmware via the ADNL Protocol\n4: \n5: ADNL is a new version of the firmware protocol. Unlike Optimus, in ADNL all commands are implemented through USB read/write, without additional USB requests (like `REQ_WRITE_MEM`, `REQ_TPL_CMD`).\n6: \n7: Just like Optimus, the ADNL protocol is implemented in IPL (BootROM), SPL (BL2), and TPL (U-Boot) bootloaders.\n8: \n9: The firmware algorithm is similar to the Optimus protocol:\n10: \n11: 1. **[IPL]** To load the new SPL into the device’s memory, first send the `download:00010000` command, followed by the file itself. The value `00010000` represents the size of the data being sent. Control is transferred to the new SPL with the `boot` command.\n12: 1. **[SPL]** Load and transfer control to the new TPL:\n13:    1. Set the `burnsteps` variable to `0xc0040002` with the `setvar:burnsteps` command.\n14:    1. Write the new TPL into the device's memory. The TPL is written using CBW (Control Block Word ?). CBW is a structure stored on the device that describes the data being received. CBW looks like this:\n15:       | Offset | Name              |\n16:       |--------|-------------------|\n17:       | 0x00   | magic ('AMLC')    |\n18:       | 0x04   | sequence          |\n19:       | 0x08   | size              |\n20:       | 0x0c   | offset            |\n21:       | 0x10   | checksum_disabled |\n22:       | 0x11   | done              |\n23: \n24:       It is assumed that CBW is filled depending on burnsteps, which was set in the first step. CBW can be obtained with the getvar:cbw command. Thus, the writing algorithm looks like this:\n25:       1. Get CBW by sending the `getvar:cbw` command.\n26:       1. If the `done` field is not `0`, it means the new file is loaded into the device's memory.\n27:       1. Write `size` bytes of data from the new BL2 at the `offset` from the CBW structure with the `download:<size>` command.\n28:       1. Check the checksum of the data sent to the device by sending the `setvar:checksum` command.\n29:       1. Go back to step 1.\n30:    1. There is no direct command to transfer control to the new TPL. It is assumed that after the entire file is transferred, BL2 itself transfers control to it (possibly depending on `burnsteps`).\n31: 1. **[TPL]** Firmware of partitions:\n32:    1. Send the [`oem disk_initial <erase>`](OPTIMUS.md#2-writing-partitions-to-disk).\n33:    1. To provide information about the firmware partition, use the command: [`oem mwrite <image_size> <image_type> <media_type> <partition>`](OPTIMUS.md#2-writing-partitions-to-disk).\n34:    1. Send the partition to the device in pieces in the following order::\n35:       1. Send the `mwrite:verify=addsum` command.\n36:       1. If the previous command returned the string `OKAY`, then the partition recording is successfully completed.\n37:       1. If the previous command returned a string in the format `DATAOUT<size><offset>`, then read from the file at the `<offset>` of `<size>` bytes of data and send to the device.\n38:       1. Read the checksum of the sent piece of data, and send the checksum (4 bytes) to the device.\n39:       1. Go back to step 1.\n40:    1. If necessary, check the checksum of the partition written to the device with the [`oem verify sha1sum <chksum>`](OPTIMUS.md#2-writing-partitions-to-disk)."}
{"step_index":1352,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-05T14:26:09Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-05T08:26:09-06:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-05T08:26:09-06:00\nShowing lines 1-553 of 553\n1: #!/usr/bin/env python3\n2: # SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0 OR MIT\n3: # -*- coding: utf-8 -*-\n4: \n5: __license__ = \"GPL-2.0\"\n6: __author__ = \"Arseniy Krasnov\"\n7: __email__ = \"avkrasnov@salutedevices.com\"\n8: __copyright__ = \"Copyright (c) 2024, SaluteDevices\"\n9: __version__ = '0.0.1'\n10: \n11: import logging\n12: import time\n13: \n14: from enum import IntEnum\n15: from types import DynamicClassAttribute\n16: \n17: import usb.core\n18: import usb.util\n19: \n20: ADNL_REPLY_OKAY = 'OKAY'\n21: ADNL_REPLY_FAIL = 'FAIL'\n22: ADNL_REPLY_INFO = 'INFO'\n23: ADNL_REPLY_DATA = 'DATA'\n24: \n25: USB_IO_TIMEOUT_MS = 5000\n26: USB_BULK_SIZE = 16384\n27: USB_READ_LEN = 512\n28: \n29: AMLOGIC_VENDOR_ID = 0x1b8e\n30: AMLOGIC_PRODUCT_ID = 0xc004\n31: \n32: BOOTROM_BURNSTEPS_0 = 0xC0040000\n33: BOOTROM_BURNSTEPS_1 = 0xC0040001\n34: BOOTROM_BURNSTEPS_2 = 0xC0040002\n35: BOOTROM_BURNSTEPS_3 = 0xC0040003\n36: \n37: TPL_BURNSTEPS_0 = 0xC0041030\n38: TPL_BURNSTEPS_1 = 0xC0041031\n39: TPL_BURNSTEPS_2 = 0xC0041032\n40: \n41: \n42: class Stage(IntEnum):\n43:     \"\"\"\n44:     Enum with boot stages of Amlogic SoC.\n45:     \"\"\"\n46:     ROM = 0\n47:     SPL = 8\n48:     TPL = 16\n49: \n50:     @DynamicClassAttribute\n51:     def name(self):\n52:         \"\"\"\n53:         Method provides custom mapping between Enum member and\n54:         user-friendly name of the boot stage in terms of Amlogic.\n55:         \"\"\"\n56:         name = {\n57:             self.ROM: \"BootROM\",\n58:             self.SPL: \"BL2\",\n59:             self.TPL: \"U-Boot\",\n60:         }.get(self)\n61: \n62:         if name:\n63:             return name\n64: \n65:         # If self (i.e. Enum member) is not found in the dict, then\n66:         # get() would return None by default. Hence return default name\n67:         # of Enum member in such case.\n68:         return super().name\n69: \n70: \n71: class SocFamily(IntEnum):\n72:     \"\"\"\n73:     Map of SoC Family name to numeric ID.\n74:     \"\"\"\n75:     A1 = 0x2c\n76:     C1 = 0x30\n77:     SC2 = 0x32\n78:     C2 = 0x33\n79:     T5 = 0x34\n80:     T5D = 0x35\n81:     T7 = 0x36\n82:     S4 = 0x37\n83: \n84: \n85: class FeatSecurebootMask(IntEnum):\n86:     \"\"\"\n87:     Defines secureboot bit inside FEAT for different SoCs.\n88:     \"\"\"\n89:     A1 = 0x1\n90:     C1 = 0x1\n91:     C2 = 0x1\n92:     T5 = 0x10\n93:     T5D = 0x10\n94: \n95: \n96: class CBW:\n97:     def __init__(self, msg) -> None:\n98:         magic = msg[4:8].tobytes().decode()\n99: \n100:         if magic != 'AMLC':\n101:             raise RuntimeError('Unexpected CBW magic')\n102: \n103:         self._seq = int.from_bytes(msg[8:12], 'little')\n104:         self._size = int.from_bytes(msg[12:16], 'little')\n105:         self._offs = int.from_bytes(msg[16:20], 'little')\n106:         self._need_checksum = not int.from_bytes(msg[20:21], 'little')\n107:         self._end = msg[21]\n108: \n109:     def size(self):\n110:         return self._size\n111: \n112:     def done(self):\n113:         return self._end\n114: \n115:     def offset(self):\n116:         return self._offs\n117: \n118: \n119: def adnl_get_prefix(msg):\n120:     return msg[:4].tobytes().decode()\n121: \n122: \n123: def adnl_checksum(buf):\n124:     # This checksum is used to verify part of image, transmitted by\n125:     # USB. It is not for verifying entire partition image.\n126:     return sum(int.from_bytes(buf[i:i + 4], 'little')\n127:                for i in range(0, len(buf), 4)) & 0xffffffff\n128: \n129: \n130: def send_cmd(epout, epin, cmd, expected_res=ADNL_REPLY_OKAY):\n131:     '''\n132:     Any command reply looks like:\n133:         | header (4b) | payload |, where\n134:     * header is a kind of ack for cmd, with values: OKAY, FAIL, INFO or DATA\n135:     * payload depends on the cmd type\n136:     '''\n137:     epout.write(cmd, USB_IO_TIMEOUT_MS)\n138:     msg = epin.read(USB_READ_LEN, USB_IO_TIMEOUT_MS)\n139: \n140:     if len(msg) < 4:\n141:         raise RuntimeError(f'Too short reply: {len(msg)}')\n142: \n143:     header = adnl_get_prefix(msg)\n144: \n145:     if header != expected_res:\n146:         raise RuntimeError(f'Unexpected reply:{header} to cmd:{cmd}')\n147: \n148:     return msg\n149: \n150: \n151: def send_cmd_identify(epout, epin):\n152:     '''\n153:     Identify command reply:\n154:     * msg[4]  - protocol type: 5 - ADNL, 3 - Optimus\n155:     * msg[5]  - minor version\n156:     * msg[7]  - stage of bootstrap, see stages dict\n157:     * msg[11] - pages map\n158:     '''\n159:     msg = send_cmd(epout, epin, 'getvar:identify')\n160:     # extra checks for this type of command\n161:     if msg[4] != 0x5:\n162:         raise RuntimeError('Unexpected data in reply to \"identify\"')\n163: \n164:     return Stage(msg[7])\n165: \n166: \n167: def get_chipinfo(epout, epin, page, offset=None, nbytes=None):\n168:     \"\"\"\n169:     Chipinfo is an information, consisting of several 'pages' with the size of\n170:     64 bytes. First 4 bytes represent particular 'page', e.g.:\n171:       * chipinfo-0: is index page (00: 58444E49 ... | 'X D N I')\n172:       * chipinfo-1: is chip page  (00: 50494843 ... | 'P I H C')\n173:       * chipinfo-3: is ROM page   (00: 564D4F52 ... | 'V M O R')\n174: \n175:     By default, function returns whole 'page', otherwise - the requested\n176:     'nbytes' from specified 'offset' inside the 'page'.\n177:     \"\"\"\n178:     stage = send_cmd_identify(epout, epin)\n179:     if stage not in (Stage.ROM, Stage.SPL):\n180:         raise RuntimeError(f\"chipinfo-{page} can't be queried from \"\n181:                            f\"stage:{stage.name}. Programmer error.\")\n182: \n183:     if not 0 <= page <= 7:\n184:         raise RuntimeError(f\"page index:{page} is out of range [0, 7]\")\n185: \n186:     # Cut off header of reply msg\n187:     msg = send_cmd(epout, epin, f\"getvar:getchipinfo-{page}\")[4:]\n188:     if offset is None:\n189:         offset = 0\n190:     if nbytes is None:\n191:         nbytes = msg.buffer_info()[1]\n192:     if offset > 0 and offset + nbytes >= msg.buffer_info()[1]:\n193:         raise RuntimeError(\"Bad parameters: out of bound access\")\n194: \n195:     return msg[offset : offset + nbytes]\n196: \n197: \n198: def adnl_get_feat(epout, epin):\n199:     \"\"\"\n200:     FEAT is 4 bytes value, residing in 'chipinfo-1'-page. Sometimes FEAT is\n201:     printed out by bootROM or SPL into UART. This value consists of flags.\n202:     \"\"\"\n203:     feat = get_chipinfo(epout, epin, 1, offset=0x24, nbytes=4)\n204:     return int.from_bytes(feat, \"little\")\n205: \n206: \n207: def adnl_get_soc_family_id(epout, epin):\n208:     \"\"\"\n209:     SoC Family is 4 byte value from 'chipinfo-1'-page.\n210:     \"\"\"\n211:     soc_fid = get_chipinfo(epout, epin, 1, offset=0x4, nbytes=4)\n212:     return SocFamily(int.from_bytes(soc_fid, \"little\"))\n213: \n214: \n215: def is_secureboot_enabled(epout, epin):\n216:     stage = send_cmd_identify(epout, epin)\n217: \n218:     if stage != Stage.ROM:\n219:         raise RuntimeError(\n220:             f\"Non suitable stage:{stage.name} for 'secureboot' query\"\n221:         )\n222: \n223:     feat = adnl_get_feat(epout, epin)\n224:     soc_fid = adnl_get_soc_family_id(epout, epin)\n225:     sb_mask = FeatSecurebootMask[soc_fid.name]\n226: \n227:     logging.info(\"SoC family '%s' (%#x): FEAT is %#x, secureboot mask:%#x\",\n228:                  soc_fid.name, soc_fid, feat, sb_mask)\n229: \n230:     return feat & sb_mask\n231: \n232: \n233: def send_burnsteps(epout, epin, burnstep):\n234:     send_cmd(epout, epin, 'setvar:burnsteps', ADNL_REPLY_DATA)\n235: \n236:     # 'burnsteps' needs extra argument\n237:     send_cmd(epout, epin, burnstep.to_bytes(4, 'little'))\n238: \n239: def tpl_burn_partition(part_item, aml_img, epout, epin):\n240:     part_name = part_item.sub_type()\n241:     logging.info('Burning partition \"%s\"', part_name)\n242:     # To burn partition, first send the following command:\n243:     # 'oem mwrite <partition size> normal store <partition name>'\n244:     # Reply must be 'OKAY'.\n245:     oem_cmd = f'oem mwrite 0x{part_item.size():x} normal store {part_name}'\n246:     send_cmd(epout, epin, oem_cmd)\n247: \n248:     while True:\n249:         # Partition is sent step by step, each step starts from\n250:         # command 'mwrite:verify=addsum', reply is 'DATAOUTX:Y'.\n251:         # X is number of bytes, which device expects in this step.\n252:         # Y is offset in the partition image. Both X and Y are in\n253:         # hex format. If reply is 'OKAY' instead of 'DATAOUTX:Y',\n254:         # then current step is done. After both 'X' and 'Y' are\n255:         # received, 'X' number of bytes are sent by blocks, each\n256:         # block is 16KB max. After 'X' bytes are transmitted,\n257:         # control sum packet is sent. It is trimmed by 4 bytes.\n258:         # Valid reply for checksum is 'OKAY'. Step is done, now\n259:         # go to this step again to send rest of partition.\n260:         # After entire parition is sent, checksum verification for\n261:         # just transmitted partition is performed. To do this,\n262:         # client sends 'oem verify sha1sum X', where 'X' is SHA1\n263:         # hash for the whole parition image (currently only SHA1\n264:         # is supported). In case of successful verification,\n265:         # device replies 'OKAY'.\n266: \n267:         epout.write('mwrite:verify=addsum', USB_IO_TIMEOUT_MS)\n268:         msg = epin.read(USB_READ_LEN, USB_IO_TIMEOUT_MS)\n269:         strmsg = msg.tobytes().decode()\n270: \n271:         if strmsg.startswith(ADNL_REPLY_OKAY):\n272:             logging.info('Burning is done')\n273:             break\n274: \n275:         if not strmsg.startswith('DATAOUT'):\n276:             raise RuntimeError(\n277:                 f'Unexpected reply to \"mwrite:verify=addsum\": {strmsg}')\n278: \n279:         size_offs = strmsg[7:].split(':')\n280:         size = int(size_offs[0], 16)\n281:         offs = int(size_offs[1], 16)\n282: \n283:         part_item.seek(offs)\n284:         buf = part_item.read(size)\n285:         sum_res = adnl_checksum(buf)\n286:         buf_offs = 0\n287: \n288:         while size > 0:\n289:             to_send = min(size, USB_BULK_SIZE)\n290:             epout.write(buf[buf_offs:buf_offs + to_send], USB_IO_TIMEOUT_MS)\n291:             size -= to_send\n292:             buf_offs += to_send\n293: \n294:         bytes_sum = [(sum_res >> i) & 0xff for i in range(0, 32, 8)]\n295: \n296:         try:\n297:             send_cmd(epout, epin, bytes_sum)\n298:         except RuntimeError as e:\n299:             raise RuntimeError('CRC error during tx') from e\n300: \n301:     # get 'VERIFY' entry for this partition\n302:     verify_item = aml_img.item_get('VERIFY', part_name)\n303:     sha1sum_str = f'oem verify {verify_item.read().decode(\"utf-8\")}'\n304:     logging.info('Verifying partition checksum using SHA1...')\n305:     epout.write(sha1sum_str)\n306: \n307:     strmsg = ''\n308: \n309:     while strmsg != ADNL_REPLY_OKAY:\n310:         logging.info('Waiting reply...')\n311:         msg = epin.read(USB_READ_LEN, USB_IO_TIMEOUT_MS)\n312:         strmsg = adnl_get_prefix(msg)\n313: \n314:         if strmsg == ADNL_REPLY_INFO:\n315:             # Device is busy because of processing checksum\n316:             time.sleep(1)\n317:             continue\n318: \n319:         if strmsg != ADNL_REPLY_OKAY:\n320:             raise RuntimeError('CRC error for partition')\n321: \n322:     logging.info('OK')\n323: \n324: \n325: def send_and_handle_cbw(epout, epin):\n326:     # CBW seems to be Control Block Word. This structure is used\n327:     # during SPL stage. Devices requests blocks of TPL image\n328:     # using this structure.\n329:     logging.info('Requesting CBW...')\n330:     msg = send_cmd(epout, epin, 'getvar:cbw')\n331: \n332:     return CBW(msg)\n333: \n334: \n335: def run_bootrom_stage(epout, epin, aml_img, has_secureboot):\n336:     (sub_type, boot_type) = (\n337:         (\"DDR_ENC\", \"secure\") if has_secureboot else (\"DDR\", \"normal\")\n338:     )\n339: \n340:     logging.info(\"Device's %s boot is in progress...\", boot_type)\n341: \n342:     item = aml_img.item_get('USB', sub_type)\n343: \n344:     logging.info('Running ROM stage...')\n345:     # May be, sequence of commands below is not necessary,\n346:     # but as from the device side there is closed ROM code\n347:     # which replies to this commands, let's follow with these\n348:     # commands as in vendor's code.\n349:     send_cmd(epout, epin, 'getvar:serialno')\n350:     send_cmd(epout, epin, 'getvar:getchipinfo-1')\n351:     send_cmd(epout, epin, 'getvar:getchipinfo-0')\n352:     send_cmd(epout, epin, 'getvar:getchipinfo-1')\n353:     send_cmd(epout, epin, 'getvar:getchipinfo-2')\n354:     send_cmd(epout, epin, 'getvar:getchipinfo-3')\n355:     send_burnsteps(epout, epin, BOOTROM_BURNSTEPS_0)\n356:     send_cmd(epout, epin, 'getvar:getchipinfo-1')\n357:     send_burnsteps(epout, epin, BOOTROM_BURNSTEPS_1)\n358: \n359:     # Preparing to send SPL (e.g. BL2)\n360:     msg = send_cmd(epout, epin, 'getvar:downloadsize')\n361: \n362:     # Reply is null-terminated\n363:     bl2_size = int(msg.tobytes().split(b'\\x00', 1)[0][4:], 0)\n364: \n365:     logging.info('Send download size:0x{:08x} for BL2'.format(bl2_size))\n366:     # Despite another size of image, send only part of whole image with the\n367:     # size, extracted by 'downloadsize' cmd - seems ROM code works only with\n368:     # this value.\n369:     send_cmd(epout, epin, 'download:{:08x}'.format(bl2_size), ADNL_REPLY_DATA)\n370: \n371:     logging.info('Sending SPL image...')\n372:     send_cmd(epout, epin, item.read())\n373:     logging.info('Done')\n374: \n375:     send_burnsteps(epout, epin, BOOTROM_BURNSTEPS_2)\n376: \n377:     logging.info('Send boot cmd')\n378:     send_cmd(epout, epin, 'boot')\n379: \n380: \n381: def run_bl2_stage(epout, epin, aml_img, has_secureboot):\n382:     # This stage writes to sticky register, then sends U-boot image\n383:     # to the device and runs it. U-boot sees value in this sticky reg\n384:     # and enters USB gadget mode to continue ADNL burning process.\n385:     logging.info('Running BL2 stage...')\n386: \n387:     # First, check that we are in SPL stage\n388:     stage = send_cmd_identify(epout, epin)\n389:     if stage != Stage.SPL:\n390:         raise RuntimeError(\n391:             f'Stage:{stage.name}. Seems, BL2 has not been booted yet. '\n392:             'Probably, you are trying to boot for example the unsigned '\n393:             'BL2 on securebooted device. Check your image, please'\n394:         )\n395: \n396:     logging.info('Send burnsteps after BL2')\n397:     send_burnsteps(epout, epin, BOOTROM_BURNSTEPS_3)\n398: \n399:     sub_type = 'UBOOT_ENC' if has_secureboot else 'UBOOT'\n400:     item = aml_img.item_get('USB', sub_type)\n401: \n402:     while True:\n403:         # request cbw\n404:         cbw = send_and_handle_cbw(epout, epin)\n405: \n406:         size = cbw.size()\n407: \n408:         if cbw.done() != 0:\n409:             logging.info('TPL sending is done')\n410:             break\n411: \n412:         item.seek(cbw.offset())\n413:         buf = item.read(size)\n414:         buf_offs = 0\n415:         cur_sum = 0\n416: \n417:         while size > 0:\n418:             to_send = min(size, USB_BULK_SIZE)\n419:             send_cmd(epout, epin, f'download:{to_send:08x}', ADNL_REPLY_DATA)\n420: \n421:             try:\n422:                 send_cmd(epout, epin, buf[buf_offs:buf_offs + to_send])\n423:             except RuntimeError as e:\n424:                 raise RuntimeError('Data tx failed') from e\n425: \n426:             cur_sum += adnl_checksum(buf[buf_offs:buf_offs + to_send])\n427:             size -= to_send\n428:             buf_offs += to_send\n429: \n430:         send_cmd(epout, epin, 'setvar:checksum', ADNL_REPLY_DATA)\n431: \n432:         bytes_sum = [(cur_sum >> i) & 0xff for i in range(0, 32, 8)]\n433: \n434:         try:\n435:             send_cmd(epout, epin, bytes_sum)\n436:         except RuntimeError as e:\n437:             raise RuntimeError('CRC error during tx') from e\n438: \n439:         logging.info('Sending CRC done')\n440: \n441: \n442: def tpl_send_burnsteps(epout, epin, second_arg):\n443:     send_cmd(epout, epin, f'oem setvar burnsteps {hex(second_arg)}')\n444: \n445: \n446: def get_device_eps(dev):\n447:     cfg = dev.get_active_configuration()\n448:     intf = cfg[(0, 0)]\n449:     direction = usb.util.endpoint_direction\n450:     # match the first OUT endpoint\n451:     epout = usb.util.find_descriptor(intf, custom_match=lambda e:\n452:                                      direction(e.bEndpointAddress) ==\n453:                                      usb.util.ENDPOINT_OUT)\n454:     # match the first IN endpoint\n455:     epin = usb.util.find_descriptor(intf, custom_match=lambda e:\n456:                                     direction(e.bEndpointAddress) ==\n457:                                     usb.util.ENDPOINT_IN)\n458: \n459:     return [epout, epin]\n460: \n461: \n462: def wait_for_device(last_dev_addr):\n463:     while True:\n464:         dev = usb.core.find(idVendor=AMLOGIC_VENDOR_ID,\n465:                             idProduct=AMLOGIC_PRODUCT_ID, backend=None)\n466: \n467:         # Uboot reenables USB on the device and enters gadget mode\n468:         # again, so wait until device appears on the USB bus with\n469:         # another address.\n470:         if dev is not None:\n471:             if dev.address != last_dev_addr:\n472:                 logging.info('Device found')\n473:                 return dev\n474: \n475:         logging.info('Waiting for the device...')\n476:         time.sleep(1)\n477: \n478: \n479: def run_tpl_stage(reset, erase_code, aml_img, dev_addr_rom_stage):\n480:     # This stage runs, when Uboot is executed on the device.\n481:     # It burns partitions (rom and spl doesn't touch storage)\n482:     # and verifies them.\n483:     logging.info('Running TPL stage...')\n484: \n485:     dev = wait_for_device(dev_addr_rom_stage)\n486: \n487:     epout, epin = get_device_eps(dev)\n488: \n489:     logging.info('Sending identify...')\n490: \n491:     send_cmd_identify(epout, epin)\n492: \n493:     tpl_send_burnsteps(epout, epin, TPL_BURNSTEPS_0)\n494:     tpl_send_burnsteps(epout, epin, TPL_BURNSTEPS_1)\n495:     send_cmd(epout, epin, f'oem disk_initial {erase_code}')\n496:     tpl_send_burnsteps(epout, epin, TPL_BURNSTEPS_2)\n497: \n498:     has_bootloader = False\n499: \n500:     for item in aml_img.items():\n501:         if item.main_type() == 'PARTITION':\n502:             has_bootloader = (item.sub_type() == 'bootloader')\n503:             tpl_burn_partition(item, aml_img, epout, epin)\n504: \n505:     if has_bootloader:\n506:         logging.info('Sending save_setting...')\n507:         send_cmd(epout, epin, 'oem save_setting')\n508: \n509:     if reset:\n510:         logging.info('Reset')\n511:         send_cmd(epout, epin, 'reboot')\n512: \n513: \n514: def do_adnl_burn(reset, erase_code, aml_img):\n515:     logging.basicConfig(level=logging.INFO,\n516:                         format='[ANDL] %(message)s')\n517:     logging.info('Looking for USB device...')\n518: \n519:     try:\n520:         dev = usb.core.find(idVendor=AMLOGIC_VENDOR_ID,\n521:                             idProduct=AMLOGIC_PRODUCT_ID, backend=None)\n522:     except usb.core.NoBackendError:\n523:         logging.error('Please install libusb')\n524:         raise\n525: \n526:     if dev is None:\n527:         logging.info('Device not found')\n528:         return\n529: \n530:     dev_addr_rom_stage = dev.address\n531: \n532:     logging.info('Setting up USB device')\n533:     epout, epin = get_device_eps(dev)\n534: \n535:     stage = send_cmd_identify(epout, epin)\n536: \n537:     if stage == Stage.TPL:\n538:         send_cmd(epout, epin, 'reboot-romusb')\n539: \n540:         dev = wait_for_device(dev_addr_rom_stage)\n541:     elif stage != Stage.ROM:\n542:         raise RuntimeError(f'Unknown stage: {stage.name}')\n543: \n544:     dev_addr_rom_stage = dev.address\n545:     epout, epin = get_device_eps(dev)\n546: \n547:     has_secureboot = is_secureboot_enabled(epout, epin)\n548: \n549:     run_bootrom_stage(epout, epin, aml_img, has_secureboot)\n550:     run_bl2_stage(epout, epin, am